      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Persons susceptible to barodontalgia include those with peridontal abscesses, carious teeth, maxillary sinus congestion, or those who have had recent extractions or restorations. A 38-year-old man had acute pain while he was in a depressurized chamber. Treatment of a periodontal abscess alleviated the problem."},
